{"test_id": "B06-007", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B06", "input": {"question": "How does penetration testing complement vulnerability scanning for CII security?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Tests exploitation chains not visible to scanners", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.2.3"}, {"fact": "Validates defense-in-depth through attack paths", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.2.3"}, {"fact": "Identifies process and human factor vulnerabilities", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.2.3"}], "expected_response": "The primary security intent of CCoP 2.0 Section 6.2.3 regarding penetration testing - validation of controls is: Validate control effectiveness through adversarial simulation.\n\nThis intent is achieved through:\n- Tests exploitation chains not visible to scanners (critical)\n- Validates defense-in-depth through attack paths (critical)\n- Identifies process and human factor vulnerabilities (important)\n\n\nUnderstanding control intent helps in implementing effective security measures that address the underlying threat rather than merely satisfying checkbox requirements. Organizations should consider both the letter and spirit of each control.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 6.2.3", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify the control specified in CCoP 2.0 6.2.3", "Extract the security objective or threat being addressed", "Analyze how the control mechanism achieves its security purpose"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating control purpose incorrectly for penetration testing - validation of controls", "Confusing control mechanism with control intent", "Attributing wrong security objectives to the control", "The security intent or objective of the control", "How the control achieves its security purpose", "The threat or risk the control addresses"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing intent not aligned with CCoP 2.0 principles", "Creating non-existent security objectives"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.2.3"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "intent_analysis", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B06-008", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B06", "input": {"question": "Why does CCoP require periodic restoration testing in addition to regular backups?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Unverified backups may fail to restore", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.6.1"}, {"fact": "Tests RTO/RPO achievement in practice", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.6.1"}, {"fact": "Validates backup integrity and completeness", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.6.1"}], "expected_response": "The primary security intent of CCoP 2.0 Section 5.6.1 regarding backup testing - recovery assurance is: Ensure actual recovery capability, not just backup creation.\n\nThis intent is achieved through:\n- Unverified backups may fail to restore (critical)\n- Tests RTO/RPO achievement in practice (critical)\n- Validates backup integrity and completeness (important)\n\n\nUnderstanding control intent helps in implementing effective security measures that address the underlying threat rather than merely satisfying checkbox requirements. Organizations should consider both the letter and spirit of each control.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 5.6.1", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify the control specified in CCoP 2.0 5.6.1", "Extract the security objective or threat being addressed", "Analyze how the control mechanism achieves its security purpose"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating control purpose incorrectly for backup testing - recovery assurance", "Confusing control mechanism with control intent", "Attributing wrong security objectives to the control", "The security intent or objective of the control", "How the control achieves its security purpose", "The threat or risk the control addresses"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing intent not aligned with CCoP 2.0 principles", "Creating non-existent security objectives"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.6.1"],